  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ernst and Young obligated $310M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Ernst and Young won 92 awards, and the average award size was $3.4M. Ernst and Young obligations fell 29.6% year over year. Ernst and Young obligations peaked in FY24 at $560M and then moved to $440M in FY25 before reaching $310M in FY26. Ernst and Young received $162M from the Department of Defense and $45.9M from the General Services Administration in FY2026 to date. Ernst and Young sold primarily accounting services, with Offices of Certified Public Accountants accounting for $274M of FY2026 to date obligations. Ernst and Young also recorded $21.9M in Other Computer Related Services and smaller amounts in several professional services and software categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Ernst and Young's federal contracting trended year over year?",
        "body": "Ernst and Young obligations peaked at $560M in FY24 and then declined to $440M in FY25. Ernst and Young obligated $310M in FY26 to date, and Ernst and Young obligations fell 29.6% year over year. Ernst and Young won 92 awards in the current fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Ernst and Young's biggest federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Ernst and Young's largest buyer at $162M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration purchased $45.9M and the Department of Housing and Urban Development purchased $35.7M. Offices of Certified Public Accountants is Ernst and Young's largest market at $274M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $21.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Ernst and Young make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Ernst and Young obligated $310M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Ernst and Young won 92 awards in the fiscal year to date and the average award size was $3.4M. Ernst and Young obligations fell 29.6% year over year."
